{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Round 3 outcomes (code-truth checks + census)\n\n### Operator rulings received\n- P11 APPROVED, hard cutover, no aliases; docs must be accurate; release notes list what breaks.\n- P13 APPROVED with revisions: real package (delete by-path loaders), extract guarded pass core so the library/MCP in-process path acquires the pass lock + heartbeat + pause + last-pass (today `_lib_ops._bridge_run` -> `run_pass_result` skips them: MCP bridge_sync runs an unlocked live pass), collapse only the middle subprocess hop (`_bridge_runner` -> `rebar bridge sync` -> `python -m rebar_reconciler`; outer 3600s kill orphans the grandchild). Subprocess boundary itself stays (no ADR ever chose it; reversing needs an ADR: 106 print sites -> logging, cooperative deadline, BaseException classification, env-vs-snapshot precedence). RP11 favoured end state = package + thin subprocess entry.\n- P16 APPROVED incl. removing tombstoned entries as a one-time documented break.\n- P17 REJECTED (confirmed by code: 16 verdicts = 5 staleness axes x distinct remediation cost; bugfix_size_gate.ACCEPTED_VERDICTS and PlanValidityProfile.CLOSE branch on code-vs-material; bug cluster is op-cert layer/hash basis/store freshness; staleness triggers ~8.5% of re-reviews, 60% are BLOCK->revise). Residue APPROVED if independently dead — confirmed on origin/main via Serena + git grep: `_hash_basis(at_current_gate_ref=)` branch (test-only callers; re-anchor test_ref_coherence on gate_ref_hash_basis), `read_set.terraform_membership_entries` (one unit test; flag ADR 0115 deferred follow-on), CLOSE/DRIFT_REFRESH profiles identical (only `profile is DEFAULT` at attest.py:683), duplicated unresolvable-ref message (attest.py:444/484), `not-closed` unreachable from plan_review_status (completion-verifier arm only). `_legacy_material_ok` is LIVE (keep). Delta explainers (resign._material_delta, generation._own/_related_material_delta, material_diff.explain_material_change) = duplication, optional separate story.\n- P19 APPROVED after verification: repo-root `bridge_state/` snapshots/sync-log/alerts/sync-route manifest have no retention; `pass_record`/`health` writers already removed (fe5a447, ADR 0094); snapshot is a same-pass round-trip (fetcher.py:630 -> load_phase.py:227), next pass diffs against committed `.bridge_state/prev_snapshot.json` key-set; client at 1,000 issues hourly ~0.8 GB/day. Fix: keep-last-N mirroring RETAIN_PER_TICKET idiom; rename ephemeral dir (9 src, 45 test files, .gitignore:14, ADR 0099:72, stale reconcile.py:150 docstring). No open ticket owns it.\n\n### P12 (RP08) — code-truth result\nRP08 rejection (dartfrog #13/#14) rests on topaz-blubbery-mice (\"we deliberately do NOT generate the surfaces (Pattern A)… adapters carry irreducible hand-written value\") and ruinable-cozey-caracal (CLI REFUSES inadmissible reason exit 1; library DISCARDS, exit 0). Revisit bar = post-oracle escape; met once: lowly-lawrencium-ovenbird (2026-09-02, _mcp_models under-declared 41 schema properties) — an outputSchema escape. ADR 0100 §2 non-derivable CLI cases stand (inline --force[=reason], arity-dispatched positionals, -- re-injection, non-argparse exit codes). Verdict: REJECT P12-full; STAGE P12-narrow (MCP only): (1) annotate 84 library params (additive), (2) load MCP outputSchemas from schemas/*.json behind a diff test, amend schemas for cross_session_warning/push_status, decide null-vs-absent (bug 3a02) — retires _mcp_models 615 + check_mcp_models 174; (3) derive the 48 library-backed tools from signatures with an override table (10 divergences, repo_root strip, descriptions, hooks); 16 mcp_only tools stay hand-registered — retires parity script/test/manifest ~1,900. Needs an ADR superseding the \"no unified adapters\" clause for MCP only; CLI + ADR 0100 untouched.\n\n### P14 — WITHDRAWN (operator was right)\n\"One retry helper\" rejected 2026-06-25 (epic civil-marlin-flare: \"over-generalization of genuinely different problems\"); ADR 0103 layered the operation-level RetryBudget OVER transport floors deliberately; ADR 0107:200-203 forbids a second retry owner; ADR 0031:70-83 refused a further lock split/merge; merged lock module = 1,464 LOC vs 800 cap. Counts were inflated by category errors (a poll, a delay fn, twelve non-loop mechanisms). Transport+structured-output merge is unsafe (pre-response identical resend vs post-response different request counted against request_limit; judge.py pins the two budgets apart). Also: I conflated the STORE write lock (fcntl+mkdir, _store/lock.py) with the reconciler pass lock (git-ref CAS lease, no fcntl). Survivors: one shared MAX_BACKOFF constant; finish ADR 0103 S3 cutover (already in P8) which ends the 12-attempt PUT stacking; fold _concurrency.py (35 LOC, not a lock) into applier.\n\n### Deprecation census (origin/main @ 8ae0d11b, 64 ahead)\nRegistry already empty; 20 tombstones all mislabeled removed_in=v1.0.0; pass #4 already half-shipped in [Unreleased] under equitable-snazzy-fruitfly. REMOVE-NOW (no decision): empty alias machinery (_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES/_ALIASES/_map_legacy_env + 2 tests + gen_env_registry ref); REBAR_CANARY_HEARTBEAT_SOURCE=github-api (two releases overdue); Route.aliases/retired dead fields; internal re-export shims (_engine_support/resolver.py whole-file re-export 71 importers, reducer/_processors, gate_dispatch, lint_expr) per ADR 0111; review_workflows.py; uvicorn_graceful_seconds alias; MCP_ENV_VARS deprecated flags + dead renderer; severity dead code (decide.py:684, llm/aggregate.py) + stale prose; shadow comparators (discovery_shadow, workflow_ops shadow_compare, payload_shadow); STATUS_GATING comments; doc drift (ADR 0086:67, ticket-model.md:288, plan-review-gate.md x4, composer_edit comment, config.md tombstone list); CHANGELOG bookkeeping (828b misfiled under 0.13.0; REBAR_HLC=0 missing). OPERATOR-DECISIONS: tombstone fate (14 warn vs 6 error rows), REBAR_CONFIG_UNKNOWN_KEYS default flip, 4-hex single-quad ids, reconciler rollback levers (CREATE_ROUTE/WRITE_FACADE in P8; LOCK_STEAL), ticket_state.signature wire field, _review_ticket_impl (blocked on eval_solver which P9 keeps), pydantic-ai google-* aliases, overlay legacy list form, REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH, fail_on_severity, infra ?token=/inline PEM, removed-alias exit-code intercept, ADR 0092 amendment, close bairnly-elliptic-toad. KEEP: ~600 persisted-data read-compat sites (store format gate, v1 alias backfill, SCHEMA_VERSION folds, HMAC verify-only, binding legacy merge, sidecar v1/v2 readers, workflow DSL shims, all 9 ensure units)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788758881312881480,"uuid":"c18bf3f3-11e7-47c7-9ce4-cce91f0f50db"}